#!/bin/bash
# 714 (Sun 22 Nov 2026 17:42, Peter: "Yes and it still needs exits ... anything using goal signal? or are you doing one thing at
# a time again"). Two sessions, started together: (A) small - fix the trial page; (B) the late in-play work with EXITS, the goal
# predictor and the live match facts all used together. Paper only. No orders. Nothing deleted.
B=/root/pe-builder; mkdir -p /root/pe-sports/inplay
cat > $B/BRIEF_trialfix.md <<'BRIEF'
You are the Builder on Peter Edwards' trading server, session 20. Small job, light on memory. Read /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_league.md (HARD RULES), reports/trial_712.md and reports/trial_today.md. Edit only grid/trial.py and its test (back up first).
FAULTS on the trial page to find and fix, each with a hand-worked check in test_trial.py: (1) M6 shows 'about 0 more markets (chance of a fluke 0.0000)' after 8 bets - a rule must never clear the bar or be promoted on a handful of bets: require at least 300 settled markets AND at least 10 separate days before the bar can be cleared or the gate called, and when every bet so far has won say 'too few to test', not 0.0000; (2) T2 shows -39.8 per £100 and T3 -96.7 per £100 - check what the £ per £100 divides by (it should be the money actually staked on the settled bets, back stake or lay liability); correct it and show the stake total beside it; (3) orders against markets: say which is counted where, one line; (4) after a rule's daily stop, show how many bets were skipped by the stop for that rule, so a stopped rule's day is not read as its full day. Do not change any rule, the fill rules, or the paper entry rule. Re-write today's file after the fix and say in reports/trial_fix_714.md (under 8 lines) what was wrong and the corrected lines for T1, T2, T3, M4-M7. Commit and push: cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/trial_fix_714.md reports/trial_today.md && git commit -qm "714: trial page fixed" && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q. Then end the session.
BRIEF
cat > $B/BRIEF_inplay.md <<'BRIEF'
You are a Builder on Peter Edwards' trading server, session 21. Work in /root/pe-sports/inplay (new files, schema 'inplay'). Read first: /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_league.md (HARD RULES, STANDING RULE 708), reports/the_map.md, reports/goal_trade.md, reports/goal_signal_audit.md, reports/other_markets.md, reports/markets_recorded.md. Import the one test's fill rules, facts.py (known-at rule, each feed's measured delay), the goal predictor version 2 and its inputs from /root/pe-sports/goaltrade - do not rewrite them. Memory: 18 GB server, other things running; database-side work in chunks, one day of ticks at a time, check free memory before each big step, keep recorders, trial loop and paper trader alive.
WHERE THE DATA HAS POINTED: of 744 gaps that survive 8 years, 741 are in play, nearly all in football goals markets late on (at 80-90 minutes 'no more goals' is rated about 73% and happens 78%; at real prices since 31 Oct backing it kept £2-4 per £100). The goal predictor version 2 adds 4-5 points on unseen days. Until now these were tested apart, as bets held to the result, on prices alone. Peter's order: it needs EXITS; prices do not tell the whole story; use the goal signal and the match facts WITH it; do not do one thing at a time; do not be narrow; let the data say where the money is.
PART 1 - THE IN-PLAY MAP, PROPERLY (football first, then every sport with in-play prices): how often it happened against what the price said, for every market we hold in play (every over/under line, first-half goals, both teams to score, match result, draw no bet, double chance, correct score, half-time markets, team goals; and the newly recorded types from 21 Nov as their days add up - list them), at every clock minute band from kick-off to 95 (5-minute bands; clock only), by: current score state (level / one up / two up; goals so far against the line; goals needed for the selection to win or lose), time since the last goal, red cards where known, pre-match strength (the pre-match prices), league level, money matched - AND by the live match facts as known at that minute with their delay (shots, shots on target, dangerous attacks, corners, expected goals: last 5/10/15 minutes and whole match, each side) - AND by the goal predictor version 2's band at that minute (its ten bands). History for depth where it has in-play prices and score; recorded days for the facts and real prices. Three periods, same sign in all three, the count of cells looked at and how many gaps chance alone would give. Use only fresh prices (state the age limit) so 'time since the last trade' is not mistaken for a gap; show how much of the 80-90 minute gap survives that.
PART 2 - EXITS, because a bet held to the whistle is not a trade: for every surviving in-play gap, at real prices since 31 Oct with Betfair's in-play bet delay modelled (state the delay used per sport and show the result with and without it), run it as a TRADE: enter by taking the price on offer (backs first; lays under 5.0 only), then (a) target: out when up 5 / 10 / 20% of the stake; (b) stop: out when down 5 / 10 / 20% of the stake, filled at the real price on offer, and for a goal against (market suspended) at the first real price after it reopens - show that loss separately, it is the real risk; (c) time: out after 3 / 5 / 10 minutes or at a fixed minute; (d) green up across both outcomes against simply closing; (e) held to the result as the control. For each: share of exits by kind, £ per £100, £ a day at £40, worst day, without the best day, first half of the dates against the second. Say plainly which exit the data prefers for each gap and whether any exit beats holding.
PART 3 - TOGETHER, not one at a time: the same trades (i) only when the goal predictor says no goal is coming / (ii) skipped when it says one is / (iii) reversed (back the goal side with a target and stop) when it says one is and the price has not moved; the same with each match-fact condition from Part 1 that survived; then the predictor and the best fact together. Does using them together beat the price alone? Give the numbers side by side: price alone / + predictor / + facts / + both.
PART 4 - WHERE ELSE: the same four parts wherever in-play prices exist - tennis (set and game state if any feed gives it; otherwise price-implied state), cricket, basketball, American football, ice hockey, darts, snooker, racing in running (say what the one-second prices allow). Do not skip a sport because it is not football; say what is missing for each.
STANDING RULE 708 applies: no 'no' or 'not yet' without the opposite side, the other markets and the other exchanges tried and shown beside it.
OUTPUT /root/pe-queue/reports/inplay.md, plain English, two screens at most. Line 1: how many in-play gaps survive with fresh prices and the bet delay modelled, and £ a day at £40 for the best non-overlapping set, held and with the best exit. Line 2: does the goal predictor, the match facts, or both add to it - yes or no with the numbers. Line 3: what went onto the trial list (frozen as measured, each a TRADE with its exits where an exit won, else labelled BET). Then each survivor as a sentence a non-trader can read with its exit, then the side-by-side table, then what could not be measured. Start with what the data supports; a shortfall is stated once, with the number, not as the headline. Push a first version (football, Parts 1-3) within 5 hours, then as each sport is added: cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/inplay.md reports/trial_today.md 2>/dev/null; git commit -qm "in play: map, exits, predictor and facts together" && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q. Then end the session.
BRIEF
for n in trialfix inplay; do
cat > $B/run_$n.sh <<SH
#!/bin/bash
CL=\$(cat /root/pe-watchman/claude_path); ts=\$(date -u +%F_%H%M)
cd /root/pe-sports/$( [ $n = inplay ] && echo inplay || echo grid ) && timeout -k 60 $( [ $n = inplay ] && echo 36000 || echo 5400 ) "\$CL" -p "\$(cat /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_$n.md)" --allowedTools "Bash,Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep" --max-turns $( [ $n = inplay ] && echo 800 || echo 150 ) --output-format text > /root/pe-builder/runs/\${ts}_$n.log 2>&1
echo "$n session ended \$(date -u '+%F %H:%M') exit \$?" >> /root/pe-builder/sessions.log
SH
chmod +x $B/run_$n.sh; nohup setsid $B/run_$n.sh > /dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &
done
sleep 20
echo "trial fix: $(pgrep -fc '[r]un_trialfix.sh') | in-play: $(pgrep -fc '[r]un_inplay.sh') | map: $(pgrep -fc '[r]un_map.sh') | free memory: $(free -g | awk '/Mem/{print $7" GB of "$2}') | $(date -u +%H:%M) UTC" > /root/pe-queue/reports/running_now.md
cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/running_now.md && git commit -qm "running now" -q && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q
